ha-citrine source patch 0003 against CitrineOS v2.1.0
(4fd7599b91c2fb6e6065e7c9b94be69880cced27), applied after 0001 and 0002:
OCPP 2.1 DER control.

Upstream v2.1.0 knows the six OCPP 2.1 DER actions by name but has no schema
entries, endpoints or handlers for them: a station's ReportDERControl,
NotifyDERStartStop or NotifyDERAlarm fails schema lookup and is answered with a
FormatViolation CALLERROR, and the operator API has no route to send
SetDERControl, GetDERControl or ClearDERControl.

The patch adds:
- the DER CALL and CALLRESULT schemas to the OCPP 2.1 schema records, and the
  three CSMS-sent request schemas to the endpoint body schemas;
- POST /ocpp/2.1/smartcharging/setDERControl, getDERControl and
  clearDERControl (OCPP 2.1 only), forwarded as sent;
- request handlers that acknowledge ReportDERControl, NotifyDERStartStop and
  NotifyDERAlarm with the empty response the schema defines (the messages
  themselves are kept in OCPPMessages, as every message is), and response
  handlers that log the station's status for the three CSMS requests;
- the handlers in the SmartCharging module's list, and tests.

No database change. The App's gateway (control-policy.mjs) decides who may
send these routes and to which station.

